cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "codelang"
abstract: >-
  codelang (Chinese alias: 懂王 / dongwang) is an open-source Windows desktop
  word-lookup tool that pops up plain-Chinese, story-driven explanations for
  code English, AI/LLM terminology, Chinese internet corporate jargon, and
  programmer slang. Hold Alt + drag your mouse over any word in any Windows
  application (browser, Word, PDF, Cursor, Claude desktop, IM clients) and a
  tooltip card appears next to the cursor. Ships with 2421 hand-written entries
  across 15 categories (dev terms, AI/LLM, platforms, OS/hardware, internet
  jargon, abbreviations, slang, product/growth, basic English, cybersecurity,
  data engineering / classic ML / DB internals, HR / VC / finance, AI industry
  people). 100% local lookup, no network calls, optional LLM fallback. MIT licensed.
message: "If you use codelang in research, articles, or videos, please cite this repository."
